{
  "id": "r05",
  "text": "On April twenty seventh, twenty fifteen, Konami confirmed that Silent Hills would not continue. Here is the contemporary report carrying the statement. One word is particularly revealing: embryonic. It describes an early project, not a completed masterpiece being pulled off a shelf. The disappointment was real, but the game people were mourning was still partly the game in their heads. Kojima, del Toro, Reedus, and a very effective teaser had given them plenty to imagine. We don't need to invent a secret meeting or a hidden motive to explain why that announcement hurt. It closed off that particular collaboration. It did not announce the end of the entire Silent Hill series. Normally, a cancelled project can leave behind a trailer or a demo as a souvenir. P.T. could have become something you showed a friend with a short explanation of what might have been. But the distribution notice had already put a deadline on the easy version of that story.",
